eepp libssh2 import, updated 2026-10-25

Upstream: https://github.com/libssh2/libssh2
Revision: 6e7b2076a6ced2230968b27ee7c1abb77fe5a88d (2026-10-24)
Version: 1.11.2_DEV, an unreleased snapshot, not a 1.11.2 release.
Source archive: https://codeload.github.com/libssh2/libssh2/tar.gz/6e7b2076a6ced2230968b27ee7c1abb77fe5a88d

Imported src/*.c, src/*.h, include/*.h, COPYING, README and RELEASE-NOTES.
The static configuration is generated by eepp's Premake build rather than by
upstream CMake/autotools. The removed crypto.c umbrella is replaced upstream
by independently compiled, backend-guarded implementation files.

Local integration retained:
- src/libssh2_config.h: platform configuration for the Premake build.
- src/mbedtls.c and src/mbedtls.h: retain the classic Mbed TLS 3.x digest,
  HMAC and CTR-DRBG APIs. eepp disables PSA; enabling shared PSA key slots
  without platform-wide threading support would change concurrency behavior.
  The adapter retains the previous per-operation allocation model, frees
  failed hash initialization, and validates digest output sizes.
- src/mbedtls_ed25519.c: Monocypher-backed Ed25519 and X25519, adapted to
  upstream's renamed private interfaces and unified private-key parser.
  Public key method strings are now NUL terminated as required upstream.
- src/mbedtls.c: OpenSSH Ed25519 public-key extraction fallback, for file
  and in-memory private keys when the .pub file is not supplied.
- .clang-format: preserve vendor formatting and macro continuations.

This snapshot incorporates the transport, ETM, SFTP lifetime, OpenSSL GCM,
publickey and authentication-length fixes identified in the security audit,
as well as subsequent upstream security fixes. Modern upstream defaults
also disable legacy SHA1/MD5/DSA algorithms; legacy-only servers can fail
negotiation rather than silently restoring weak algorithms.

Validation and remaining work are recorded in docs/security/.
